      "message": "interrupt_unlock() will call \u0027sti\u0027 to enable interrupts, it\u0027s dangerous when calling ish_dma_init() which will call here in system init stage before task_start().\n\nin fact, i already met strange crash issues when doing ish_dma_init() in ish_pm_init() which called by system_pre_init(), the crash issues caused by interrupts generated before task_start(), it triggerd task switch, but the kernel status are unknown before task_start().\n\nso i made a W/A in power_mgt.c for this issue. \nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1531772/3/chip/ish/power_mgt.c#449    \n\nlike all other drivers,  their init function all got called in main() before task_start().\n\nso we need make sure ish_dma_init() function should not enable interrupt.",
